  "seoTitle": "PT Fonusa Agung Mulia Fire Victims Identification Update",
  "metaDescription": "Authorities have identified twenty-seven victims of the PT Fonusa Agung Mulia factory fire as search operations continue at the damaged site in Cikande.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "Disaster victim identification teams have confirmed the identities of twenty-seven individuals following the fire at the Cikande facility.",
    "Ongoing search efforts are currently being hindered by hazardous debris and unstable building structures at the factory site.",
    "Police have upgraded the case status to a formal investigation amid allegations of safety violations regarding occupational health and labor standards."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The fire at the PT Fonusa Agung Mulia candy factory in Cikande, Serang, has led to a major search and identification operation that has entered its fourth day. Rescue teams are navigating complex conditions, including dangerous building debris and inclement weather, such as lightning, which has slowed progress. Some recovered remains have been preserved in freezers to facilitate the ongoing identification process. Meanwhile, law enforcement agencies have officially escalated the incident to a criminal investigation, citing preliminary evidence of negligence. Labor representatives have publicly alleged that the factory violated workplace safety regulations and have demanded substantial compensation for the victims. Authorities continue to work toward identifying all affected individuals while simultaneously securing the structural integrity of the affected manufacturing site to allow for further recovery operations.",
